    "text": "Part 3 of DNS & TLS FIELD HANDBOOK. Four round trips happen before your browser sends a single byte of HTTP — and most outages live in those four. This handbook walks the whole path: DNS hierarchy, delegation, glue, TTL maths and the propagation myth, then TLS 1.2 vs 1.3 handshakes, X.509 chains, cleartext SNI and ECH. Ends with the mistakes that break both and the exact dig and openssl commands that find them.",
